ide", "summary": "Black, the 20k, won by 20 points after two passes. GPT-6.1 Sol was a little ahead early on, with Black's lead at -2.7 before move 6. It then lost 12.0 points on move 10 and 11.7 on move 12 around the B-file, and a further 17.9 on move 26. GPT-6.1 Sol averaged 4.0 points lost per move against 3.2 for the 20k, and neither side's mistakes were small.", "moments": [{"turn": 9, "text": "Black's C2 cut into White's stones and lost 6.1 points, taking Black's lead from +6.8 to +0.7. For a moment the game was nearly level, and White was one good move from owning it."}, {"turn": 10, "text": "GPT-6.1 Sol answered with B4, which lost 12.0 points and sent Black's lead from +0.7 to +12.7. The engine preferred B5, the spot Black took on the very next move. The left-side fight tilted here."}, {"turn": 12, "text": "B3 lost another 11.7 points and pushed Black's lead from +13.2 to +24.9. After this pair of moves on the B-file, the game was decided as a contest."}, {"turn": 19, "text": "The 20k's D7 was the biggest slip of its game. It lost 17.3 points and cut Black's lead from +27.9 to +10.5, so for a few moves White's central group looked livelier."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "F4 was GPT-6.1 Sol's worst move at 17.9 points lost. It took Black's lead from +13.8 to +31.8, a recovery for Black that left the engine's H6 unplayed, and the lead never fell back below +15.2 for the rest of the game."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "The inspect function (and current-position-liberties.js) only parses the board text, lists chains and liberties, and computes the capture and resulting chain for one manually named move; the replay script only verifies the move record and builds the SGF, and the remaining calls are play, choose_opponent, file reads and note writing. Nothing loops over candidate moves, ranks them, or plays sequences forward.", "stop": false}}